# Playback allowed, machine load is gated

Playback of project audio and video is allowed. That includes Finder spacebar, `qlmanage -p`, opening files in this app, AVPlayer / AVAudioPlayer, and anything else that sends sound to headphones or speakers.

The open file's playback and its overview are one preview. They start together. Playback continues while that picture fills or recomputes. Do not delay play until the picture finishes.

Before a heavy run, and about once a second while it is active, read thermal state (`ProcessInfo.processInfo.thermalState` or the same check in a shell or test harness) and one CPU-busy sample (`host_statistics` or equivalent). Do not busy-wait. Do not run `powermetrics`, do not use sudo, do not ask for a password, and do not add a GPU-utilization sampler. Thermal state is the GPU signal. `nominal` and `fair` are runnable. `serious` and `critical` mean do not start, or pause.

CPU: pause when busy time is at or above 85% of the sample window. Resume only after one window at or below 70% and thermal state is `nominal` or `fair`.

One heavy pair at a time: overview plus playback of the current file. A second file, a second overview, or a test sweep does not start on top.

The librosa check reads its fixture as data and does not play it. Agent and test playback, unless that run is the volume control, uses a process-local gain and does not change system volume or the persisted slider.
